// ============================================================================
// Interactions in the boss's compound (Chapter 2): one knot per interactable in
// src/data/areas/borderland/compound.ts (the yard) and compoundHouse.ts (the
// house, inside it). Draft text for the designer to rewrite.
// ============================================================================

// --- The yard ---

=== compound_gate ===
The gate's leaves are whole and matched, and somebody cleans them. They stand open; nobody would walk in uninvited anyway.
-> END

=== compound_washing ===
Washing on a line, drying in the sun. Bright cloth, every piece whole. Nobody here wears patches.
-> END

=== compound_tank ===
A water tank. Whole, sealed, full. You could drink from it for a year.
-> END

=== compound_tribute ===
Crates under a cloth, waiting to be counted. Tonight's share, or last night's.
-> END

=== compound_windows ===
Windows with curtains, lamplight behind them, even in the day. Somebody's put flowers made of cloth in the boxes under them.
It looks like a home. That's the strangest thing about it.
-> END

// --- The house ---

=== house_pegs ===
Cloaks on pegs by the door, boots lined up underneath. Good boots, resoled more than once.
-> END

=== compound_light ===
A light that works. Not a fire, not oil: it just glows, steady, and nobody knows how.
It's the only one in the borderland, and it's his.
-> END

=== compound_table ===
Real food on the table. Bread. Greens. More than you'd see in a week.
-> END

=== house_stove ===
A stove made from some great old casing, a fire going in its belly and a pot on top. It smells of something with meat in it.
-> END

=== house_pantry ===
Shelves of jars and tins, all full. Food put by, for a bad season. You've never seen a bad season end with food left over.
-> END

=== house_side_room ===
A smaller table, stools round it, and a board on the wall covered in marks. Who owes what, and who's paid.
-> END

=== compound_locked ===
Locked. Nobody goes in, and nobody says why.
-> END

=== house_window ===
From up here you can see over the settlement's roofs, all the way to the walls. Everything, and everyone.
-> END

=== house_bed ===
A bed with a real frame, a quilt sewn from a hundred patches, two pillows. A chest at its foot, bound in metal.
-> END

=== house_trophies ===
A shelf of finds, set out to be looked at, not traded. A ring of pale casing, a slab of glass, and one small thing still glowing.
-> END

=== compound_rooms ===
Beds with frames, and blankets nobody's patched.
-> END

// --- People (draft) ---

=== compound_enforcer ===
"Nobody goes in unless they're asked. You asked?" #speaker:enforcer
-> END

=== compound_son ===
"Oh. It's you." #speaker:boss_son
"My father talks about you, you know. I can't think why." #speaker:boss_son
-> END

=== house_boss ===
"Come in, come in. Anyone who digs as hard as you is welcome at my table." #speaker:boss
"We look after our own here. Remember that." #speaker:boss
-> END

=== house_watcher ===
The watcher looks at you for a long moment, and says nothing at all.
-> END
